  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let the equation of the plane passing through the line<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65</mn></math>. Then the distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> from the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of plane through the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Also, this plane is parallel to the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, so</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>So, equation of&nbsp;plane is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn></math></p><p>So, distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>26</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> units</p>",
